TRUE(1)                        P32W Unix                         TRUE(1)

NAME
       true - do nothing, successfully

SYNOPSIS
       true

DESCRIPTION
       true does nothing and exits with status 0. Arguments are
       ignored. It is used in shell scripts, for example as the
       condition of an endless loop.

EXAMPLES
       while true; do date; sleep 60; done

EXIT STATUS
       0.

SEE ALSO
       false(1), sh(1), test(1)
